A lot of people don't take the time to call their parents while they still can, because they have their differences, because they are "busy", because they have their own problems to sort out first; 

but the older you become, the more you understand their love for you, and the more you notice how much they did for you even in awkward and confused ways; 

and as you raise your own kids, you understand how challenging it is to build a loving family in healthy conditions, and one thing becomes obvious:

if you project yourself in the future, and imagine yourself at your parents' age, or at the end of their lives, and also imagine your young kids at your current age, you suddenly get struck with the vision of how you would like to be treated one day, a vision of what a family you could have and of how things could be, and thus, you suddenly understand how you should treat your own parents if you still have the privilege to still spend a bit of time with them.
